From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Trowbridge <chris.trowbridge@ezurio.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rsa-sign: load openssl config for provider support

When OPENSSL_CONF is set, ensure OpenSSL loads the configuration file
during initialization so that providers (such as pkcs11-provider for
HSM/KMS-based signing) are activated before key loading.

Without this, PEM_read_PrivateKey() cannot decode PKCS#11 Provider URI
PEM wrappers because the pkcs11-provider decoder is never registered.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]

Signed-off-by: Chris Trowbridge <chris.trowbridge@ezurio.com>
---
 lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c b/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
+++ b/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
@@ -315,7 +315,7 @@ static int rsa_init(void)
 {
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = OPENSSL_init_ssl(0, NULL);
+	ret = OPENSSL_init_ssl(OPENSSL_INIT_LOAD_CONFIG, NULL);
 	if (!ret) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "Failure to init SSL library\n");
 		return -1;
-- 
2.44.0
